        "procedure": "EuCl3·6H2O (0.86 g, 2.36 mmol) and H4TC4A (0.28 g, 0.38 mmol) were dissolved in MeOH/DMF (24 mL, v/v = 1:1), stirred at room temperature for 5 h, then TEA (60 μL) was added. The solution was sealed in a 50 mL Teflon-lined autoclave, kept at 140 °C for two days, and slowly cooled to 30 °C at about 3 °C h−1. Colorless block-shaped crystals were isolated by filtration, washed with 1:1 MeOH–DMF, and dried in air.",
